- Yes.

516
00:18:20,953 --> 00:18:22,483
(The second dish, grilled shrimp)

517
00:18:22,483 --> 00:18:23,523
Seriously.

518
00:18:25,053 --> 00:18:26,823
(Sniffing)

519
00:18:27,163 --> 00:18:29,263
- Thank you.
- This butter smells so unique.

520
00:18:29,863 --> 00:18:31,563
- It also smells like curry.
- Yes!

521
00:18:32,233 --> 00:18:34,563
- Like Indian curry, right?
- Yes.

522
00:18:35,463 --> 00:18:37,403
(Kyung Pyo tries it first.)

523
00:18:38,373 --> 00:18:39,503
It's good.

524
00:18:43,773 --> 00:18:46,073
(While everyone is enjoying it,)

525
00:18:46,473 --> 00:18:48,913
(he's struggling.)

526
00:18:49,383 --> 00:18:50,383
(Exclaiming)

527
00:18:50,383 --> 00:18:51,653
I personally think...

528
00:18:51,983 --> 00:18:53,883
you should peel the whole shrimp if you're going to.

529
00:18:55,823 --> 00:18:58,093
I'd say I made it really easy to peel them.

530
00:18:58,093 --> 00:19:00,153
I see. You heard that?

531
00:19:00,763 --> 00:19:01,863
I guess you heard that.

532
00:19:01,863 --> 00:19:03,593
So, you're just bad at peeling shrimp.

533
00:19:04,033 --> 00:19:05,963
Most people can do it.

534
00:19:05,963 --> 00:19:08,903
I hate having to peel my food.

535
00:19:09,533 --> 00:19:11,203
(Taking a bite)

536
00:19:11,273 --> 00:19:12,903
There's a famous story.

537
00:19:13,473 --> 00:19:15,643
One day, Jae Seok invited...

538
00:19:15,643 --> 00:19:17,313
his junior comedians for a meal, so they went.

539
00:19:17,313 --> 00:19:19,743
And his mom made like 20 dishes.

540
00:19:21,083 --> 00:19:23,113
Everyone was so amazed...

541
00:19:23,113 --> 00:19:25,053
and dying to eat them, and Jae Seok suddenly said,

542
00:19:25,553 --> 00:19:26,683
"Mom, do we have ramyeon?"

543
00:19:28,483 --> 00:19:31,223
I prefer ramyeon over my mom's cooking.

544
00:19:32,223 --> 00:19:33,993
It may sound ungrateful, but...

545
00:19:33,993 --> 00:19:35,893
So, they were all shocked.

546
00:19:36,793 --> 00:19:38,463
You can put all sorts of delicacies on the table,

547
00:19:39,093 --> 00:19:41,833
and what I want at that moment is my delicacy.

548
00:19:45,403 --> 00:19:46,773
(The owner came back with something.)

549
00:19:46,773 --> 00:19:49,343
The next dish is our main steak.

550
00:19:49,873 --> 00:19:52,243
(The main dish is here.)

551
00:19:52,713 --> 00:19:54,743
That's not dry ice. It's the smell of charcoal.

552
00:19:55,143 --> 00:19:57,113
- It's smoked.
- It's so aromatic.

553
00:20:02,383 --> 00:20:03,483
(Startled)

554
00:20:03,483 --> 00:20:04,723
With the bones?

555
00:20:04,853 --> 00:20:05,923
That's bone marrow.

556
00:20:05,923 --> 00:20:08,223
- Oh, that's bone marrow?
- Yes.

557
00:20:08,223 --> 00:20:09,993
- Is that it?
- Yes.

558
00:20:10,963 --> 00:20:13,763
The third dish, the main dish, is Korean heifer steak.

559
00:20:13,763 --> 00:20:15,903
We grilled it alongside bone marrow...

560
00:20:15,903 --> 00:20:19,033
in our custom wood-fired oven.

561
00:20:19,033 --> 00:20:20,403
(Steaks and bone marrow cooked in a wood-fired oven)

562
00:20:20,403 --> 00:20:22,743
Chimichurri is a signature South American sauce...

563
00:20:22,743 --> 00:20:25,213
made with herbs and a touch of acidity.

564
00:20:25,213 --> 00:20:28,013
(A subtle smoky aroma by adding burnt rosemary)

565
00:20:29,043 --> 00:20:31,783
(The third dish, Korean heifer steak)

566
00:20:32,983 --> 00:20:34,353
Excellent.

567
00:20:34,353 --> 00:20:36,753
You can't eat steaks like this at home.

568
00:20:36,753 --> 00:20:37,823
Right.

569
00:20:37,993 --> 00:20:39,193
It smells so good.

570
00:20:40,663 --> 00:20:41,793
- That's...
- Rosemary.

571
00:20:41,793 --> 00:20:43,463
- Yes, rosemary, right?
- Yes.

572
00:20:44,593 --> 00:20:46,733
- Is that gravy?
- It is.

573
00:20:46,733 --> 00:20:48,563
(It's gravy sauce.)

574
00:20:48,763 --> 00:20:50,733
(You're so good at this!)

575
00:20:51,273 --> 00:20:53,303
- What was that, BIBI?
- You sound so smart.

576
00:20:53,703 --> 00:20:55,403
- What's this called?
- Gravy.

577
00:20:55,403 --> 00:20:56,573
- Gravy?
- Yes.

578
00:20:56,573 --> 00:20:58,173
(A bunch of gravy with that meaty flavour)

579
00:20:58,613 --> 00:21:00,943
- Heifer steak?
- It looks good.

580
00:21:01,613 --> 00:21:02,683
It's made of South American herbs...

581
00:21:02,683 --> 00:21:04,853
- Chimichurri!
- Yes, we added that.

582
00:21:05,053 --> 00:21:07,213
They all look so expensive.

583
00:21:07,523 --> 00:21:09,583
You two respond so differently.

584
00:21:09,723 --> 00:21:12,093
BIBI is so glad to see them,

585
00:21:12,093 --> 00:21:14,223
and Jae Seok is like, "They look expensive."

586
00:21:14,793 --> 00:21:16,123
"Very expensive."

587
00:21:16,123 --> 00:21:18,163
(Let's give them a try.)

588
00:21:18,463 --> 00:21:19,893
- Very expensive.
- Very expensive.

589
00:21:21,733 --> 00:21:23,033
I bet it's good.

590
00:21:23,463 --> 00:21:25,033
- And it's cooked perfectly.
- Yes.

591
00:21:25,033 --> 00:21:26,503
(It's cooked to perfection!)

592
00:21:26,803 --> 00:21:27,843
Let's find out.

593
00:21:27,843 --> 00:21:29,003
(How will it taste?)

594
00:21:29,003 --> 00:21:30,073
What do you think?

595
00:21:30,073 --> 00:21:31,073
(Moaning)

596
00:21:31,173 --> 00:21:33,113
(Satisfied)

597
00:21:33,113 --> 00:21:34,783
- Let's see.
- And it's cooked perfectly.

598
00:21:34,783 --> 00:21:36,143
- Yes.
- I'm serious.

599
00:21:37,313 --> 00:21:38,653
- Right?
- It's medium...

600
00:21:38,653 --> 00:21:40,253
(Exclaiming)

601
00:21:40,253 --> 00:21:41,423
This is the main dish.

602
00:21:41,683 --> 00:21:43,223
- Is it? The steak?
- Yes.

603
00:21:43,223 --> 00:21:44,293
It's definitely the main dish.

604
00:21:45,123 --> 00:21:47,153
(BIBI, the foodie,)

605
00:21:47,153 --> 00:21:50,123
(puts chimichurri on top.)

606
00:21:50,323 --> 00:21:51,393
- Is it? The steak?
- Yes.

607
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,533
It's definitely the main dish.

608
00:21:54,333 --> 00:21:55,333
(Laughing)

609
00:21:55,633 --> 00:21:56,963
- I knew it was good.
- How is it?

610
00:21:58,303 --> 00:22:00,873
(Happy)

611
00:22:01,243 --> 00:22:03,473
The price doesn't feel right, though.

612
00:22:04,013 --> 00:22:06,373
- Wait. How much was it?
- Right.

613
00:22:06,613 --> 00:22:08,343
The course is 98 dollars for dinner.

614
00:22:08,513 --> 00:22:10,043
- It's 98 dollars?
- That's right.

615
00:22:10,913 --> 00:22:13,013
That sounds reasonable for a full-course meal.

616
00:22:13,013 --> 00:22:14,023
- Yes.
- Right.

617
00:22:14,023 --> 00:22:16,023
I'm surprised that it's cheaper than it looks.

618
00:22:16,123 --> 00:22:18,293
When you consider the labour costs...

619
00:22:18,293 --> 00:22:19,353
Exactly.

620
00:22:19,353 --> 00:22:20,623
(The price is too low considering its quality and quantity.)

621
00:22:20,763 --> 00:22:21,963
I don't think...

622
00:22:22,363 --> 00:22:24,993
this restaurant usually serves this kind of food.

623
00:22:26,293 --> 00:22:29,603
When you look at all the equipment, there are shelves.

624
00:22:30,303 --> 00:22:33,233
Maybe they serve Texas barbecue that has to be cooked...

625
00:22:33,233 --> 00:22:34,743
on different shelves.

626
00:22:36,303 --> 00:22:37,843
(Kyung Pyo's guess)

627
00:22:37,843 --> 00:22:39,913
(It's a Texas barbecue place, not a fire show place?)

628
00:22:40,243 --> 00:22:41,313
I see.

629
00:22:41,743 --> 00:22:43,543
Meat that needs a long time to cook.

630
00:22:43,883 --> 00:22:46,083
Now that he said that,

631
00:22:46,513 --> 00:22:48,323
all he did was pour oil on top.

632
00:22:49,653 --> 00:22:52,023
He didn't actually cook.

633
00:22:52,123 --> 00:22:53,293
- Right. They all came...
- They brought it out.

634
00:22:53,293 --> 00:22:54,423
- Yes.
- from the kitchen.

635
00:22:55,723 --> 00:22:57,533
(All the dishes were already cooked...)

636
00:22:57,533 --> 00:22:59,893
(before leaving the kitchen.)

637
00:23:00,293 --> 00:23:02,303
Could he be an actor?

638
00:23:02,763 --> 00:23:04,103
- He could be.
- Maybe he is.

639
00:23:04,203 --> 00:23:06,373
Now that you say that, he said,

640
00:23:06,433 --> 00:23:09,573
"You're the audience, and I'm performing."

641
00:23:10,443 --> 00:23:12,643
(The fire tower and the kitchen are our stage.)

642
00:23:12,643 --> 00:23:14,243
(The chefs are the actors.)

643
00:23:14,583 --> 00:23:18,413
(And our customers are the audience.)

644
00:23:18,753 --> 00:23:20,983
- That might be true.
- Yes, what he said!

645
00:23:20,983 --> 00:23:22,253
He might have been telling the truth.

646
00:23:22,483 --> 00:23:24,153
He was tipping us off.

647
00:23:24,593 --> 00:23:26,653
And when we get it wrong,

648
00:23:26,753 --> 00:23:27,863
it's a great source to mock us.

649
00:23:27,863 --> 00:23:29,093
- Exactly!
- Yes.

650
00:23:29,093 --> 00:23:30,793
It's so easy for the crew to mock us.

651
00:23:30,793 --> 00:23:32,063
- They had already told us.
- He was acting...

652
00:23:32,063 --> 00:23:33,393
- on Sixth Sense.
- Yes.

653
00:23:33,533 --> 00:23:35,403
We have to keep suspecting...

654
00:23:36,563 --> 00:23:38,073
(The chef appears at that moment.)

655
00:23:38,233 --> 00:23:39,433
I never knew you'd come.

656
00:23:39,433 --> 00:23:40,973
(Flustered)

657
00:23:41,073 --> 00:23:42,873
Did he come out to correct us?

658
00:23:43,303 --> 00:23:44,343
This is our dessert.

659
00:23:44,343 --> 00:23:46,273
We have another fire show for it.

660
00:23:46,273 --> 00:23:48,143
- Is that cheese?
- No, it's dessert.

661
00:23:48,143 --> 00:23:50,013
Did you bring the meringue on purpose?

662
00:23:50,343 --> 00:23:51,713
To call us morons?

663
00:23:51,713 --> 00:23:53,113
(Are you morons?)

664
00:23:53,113 --> 00:23:55,123
- "These morons."
- You just couldn't help it.

665
00:23:56,253 --> 00:23:57,793
- It was right on time.
- You see what I mean?

666
00:23:57,793 --> 00:23:58,823
Yes.

667
00:23:58,823 --> 00:24:00,353
But the food is really delicious.

668
00:24:01,623 --> 00:24:04,993
(The chef gets ready for another fire show.)

669
00:24:04,993 --> 00:24:06,893
- Is that oil?
- It's alcohol.

670
00:24:06,893 --> 00:24:08,003
- Whiskey?
- Yes.

671
00:24:08,163 --> 00:24:09,933
(He uses fire for dessert too?)

672
00:24:10,873 --> 00:24:15,743
(A scoop of whiskey that caught on fire)

673
00:24:16,673 --> 00:24:17,743
You're putting fire on top?

674
00:24:17,743 --> 00:24:19,673
- He's burning the surface.
- Yes.

675
00:24:20,443 --> 00:24:21,683
It's called a Baked Alaska.

676
00:24:21,683 --> 00:24:24,013
The inside is filled with ice cream or cake,

677
00:24:24,153 --> 00:24:25,913
while the outer meringue layer contains air pockets...

678
00:24:25,913 --> 00:24:27,253
that act as thermal insulation.

679
00:24:27,353 --> 00:24:28,453
So, when heat is applied,

680
00:24:28,453 --> 00:24:30,823
the meringue toasts while the ice cream remains cold.

681
00:24:31,693 --> 00:24:35,093
(The final dish, Baked Alaska)

682
00:24:35,093 --> 00:24:37,563
I'll come back with your dessert.

683
00:24:37,963 --> 00:24:39,133
Why would you take it back?

684
00:24:39,133 --> 00:24:40,133
(Doubtful)

685
00:24:40,133 --> 00:24:41,133
He keeps...

686
00:24:41,663 --> 00:24:43,833
- He keeps acting suspiciously.
- Right?

687
00:24:44,173 --> 00:24:46,873
- Maybe that's all he practised.
- What do you think?

688
00:24:46,903 --> 00:24:48,643
He doesn't show us everything.

689
00:24:49,803 --> 00:24:52,143
He demonstrated on one, and now we have four.

690
00:24:52,813 --> 00:24:55,143
- That's the end of the course.
- Okay.

691
00:24:55,143 --> 00:24:57,113
The last one is our signature event.

692
00:24:57,113 --> 00:24:58,553
It's fire gazing.

693
00:24:58,553 --> 00:25:00,353
You can space out while watching the fire.

694
00:25:00,353 --> 00:25:01,353
(Thank you.)

695
00:25:01,423 --> 00:25:03,023
Thank you.

696
00:25:03,253 --> 00:25:04,793
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you.

697
00:25:04,793 --> 00:25:05,893
When he did it here,

698
00:25:05,893 --> 00:25:07,293
- it looked too burnt...
- What's happening?

699
00:25:08,563 --> 00:25:10,423
(The lights went off again.)

700
00:25:10,793 --> 00:25:13,833
(As you were leaving, you said to me)

701
00:25:14,203 --> 00:25:15,663
He's suddenly playing "Bam Yang Gang."

702
00:25:15,663 --> 00:25:17,803
(The fire gazing began with "Bam Yang Gang...")

703
00:25:17,803 --> 00:25:19,103
(in the background.)

704
00:25:20,133 --> 00:25:23,843
(Let's be mesmerized by the flames in the middle of the city.)

705
00:25:28,743 --> 00:25:30,543
You can't help but stare into the fire.

706
00:25:31,013 --> 00:25:32,553
I can't help it.

707
00:25:32,553 --> 00:25:34,183
(I love fire gazing.)

708
00:25:36,583 --> 00:25:41,793
(It's a perfect moment with some sweet dessert.)

709
00:25:43,493 --> 00:25:45,063
The fact that we can do this in the middle of the summer...

710
00:25:45,063 --> 00:25:46,163
- is fascinating.
- Yes!

711
00:25:46,163 --> 00:25:48,033
It's so romantic. I love it.

712
00:25:50,103 --> 00:25:51,573
- The temperature is...
- Just right.

713
00:25:51,573 --> 00:25:52,733
- Yes, it is.
- It's pleasant.

714
00:25:52,733 --> 00:25:54,743
(Mesmerized by the bonfire)

715
00:25:55,303 --> 00:25:56,343
When...

716
00:25:56,773 --> 00:25:58,973
couples come here, I bet they kiss.

717
00:25:59,143 --> 00:26:00,573
(Laughing)

718
00:26:00,743 --> 00:26:02,143
Is that coming from experience?

719
00:26:02,713 --> 00:26:04,283
I bet a lot of them kiss during this.

720
00:26:04,753 --> 00:26:06,513
(Watch out for this kissing gourami.)

721
00:26:06,683 --> 00:26:08,223
- You've never kissed before.
- I mean...

722
00:26:08,923 --> 00:26:11,123
You can dim the lights too.

723
00:26:11,123 --> 00:26:13,453
It'd be so funny if you added a kissing moment.

724
00:26:13,453 --> 00:26:14,493
Yes.

725
00:26:15,263 --> 00:26:16,963
- There's ice cream inside.
- Yes.

726
00:26:17,663 --> 00:26:19,633
It's smokey ice cream.

727
00:26:21,133 --> 00:26:23,163
This ice cream tastes familiar, though.

728
00:26:23,733 --> 00:26:24,903
Is this Gugu Cluster?

729
00:26:26,473 --> 00:26:28,643
- That's what it tastes like.
- Yes.

730
00:26:29,073 --> 00:26:32,013
Once it starts looking suspicious, everything looks fake.

731
00:26:32,013 --> 00:26:33,113
- Yes.
- Right?

732
00:26:33,343 --> 00:26:35,383
Every time, he does a short demonstration...

733
00:26:35,843 --> 00:26:37,883
and comes back with four dishes from the kitchen.

734
00:26:37,883 --> 00:26:39,253
(It's like magic that copies 4 dishes.)

735
00:26:39,583 --> 00:26:41,453
Why don't we move to the second one?

736
00:26:41,453 --> 00:26:42,453
- Great idea.
- Yes.

737
00:26:42,453 --> 00:26:43,483
(The fire-show restaurant)

738
00:26:43,483 --> 00:26:44,853
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you for the food!

739
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:45,893
Thank you!

740
00:26:46,553 --> 00:26:47,593
Definitely.

741
00:26:47,793 --> 00:26:49,363
- Oh, my gosh.
- Oh, my.

742
00:26:49,593 --> 00:26:50,863
- That startled me.
- Oh, man.

743
00:26:50,863 --> 00:26:52,663
When did they all go up there?

744
00:26:52,663 --> 00:26:53,693
I have no idea.

745
00:26:53,693 --> 00:26:55,703
- You're so handsome!
- Hi!

746
00:26:55,703 --> 00:26:56,903
(Citizens heard the news and came to watch.)

747
00:26:56,903 --> 00:26:58,803
- Hi, everyone.
- No way.

748
00:26:58,803 --> 00:26:59,933
I'm afraid we have to move.

749
00:26:59,933 --> 00:27:01,603
- Do we get in this van?
- Yes.

750
00:27:02,343 --> 00:27:03,543
- It's already the second one?
- Today,

751
00:27:03,543 --> 00:27:04,543
I think...

752
00:27:04,543 --> 00:27:07,273
we have to figure out if the show is real or fake.

753
00:27:07,473 --> 00:27:09,183
We have to focus on the show more than the food.

754
00:27:09,183 --> 00:27:10,843
We're easily distracted by the food.

755
00:27:11,183 --> 00:27:12,853
It looked so easy...

756
00:27:13,353 --> 00:27:14,583
to make up the performance...

757
00:27:14,583 --> 00:27:15,753
because the dishes were real.

758
00:27:15,753 --> 00:27:16,753
- Exactly.
- Yes.

759
00:27:16,753 --> 00:27:18,093
- Right?
- Right.

760
00:27:18,293 --> 00:27:19,893
It was also weird that he used a handheld torch...

761
00:27:19,893 --> 00:27:21,623
with that amazing wood fire next to him.

762
00:27:21,623 --> 00:27:23,263
- Exactly!
- Yes, that was also suspicious.

763
00:27:23,263 --> 00:27:25,993
He used that charcoal...

764
00:27:25,993 --> 00:27:27,563
- Only in the beginning.
- Right?

765
00:27:27,763 --> 00:27:29,763
He only used the torch after that.

766
00:27:29,763 --> 00:27:32,873
The performance that he did seem like anyone could pull it off...

767
00:27:33,133 --> 00:27:35,003
- after practice.
- Absolutely.

768
00:27:35,003 --> 00:27:36,043
Right.

769
00:27:36,243 --> 00:27:37,913
BIBI, did you find anything suspicious?

770
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:41,283
I was too distracted by the food.

771
00:27:41,283 --> 00:27:42,843
- Oh, no.
- You paid attention to the food.

772
00:27:42,843 --> 00:27:44,083
I couldn't notice anything else.

773
00:27:44,083 --> 00:27:46,553
I'm sorry I'm not much help.

774
00:27:46,553 --> 00:27:48,753
I was way too distracted.

775
00:27:48,753 --> 00:27:50,853
- By the food?
- By the food.

776
00:27:50,853 --> 00:27:52,723
I think I should be careful from now on.

777
00:27:52,823 --> 00:27:54,593
I'll start training.

778
00:27:54,823 --> 00:27:56,893
- How would you train?
- I'll train how to focus...

779
00:27:56,893 --> 00:28:00,063
on other things with the food in front of me.

780
00:28:00,293 --> 00:28:01,633
That won't be so easy.

781
00:28:01,633 --> 00:28:03,703
Normally, I pay attention to the food with passion.

782
00:28:03,703 --> 00:28:04,873
- Really?
- Yes.

783
00:28:06,533 --> 00:28:08,343
I think we're near Hongdae.

784
00:28:08,343 --> 00:28:09,373
We are.

785
00:28:09,943 --> 00:28:12,613
- It's going to be a good show.
- Right.

786
00:28:12,613 --> 00:28:14,913
I wonder what kind of show it is this time.

787
00:28:15,383 --> 00:28:16,913
What would be the second place?

788
00:28:17,413 --> 00:28:18,453
We'll find out.

789
00:28:18,453 --> 00:28:20,653
What was the hint about the second show?

790
00:28:21,083 --> 00:28:22,583
It was, "Something's moving!"

791
00:28:22,583 --> 00:28:23,583
- "Something's moving."
- Right.

792
00:28:23,583 --> 00:28:24,723
"It is moving!"

793
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:26,793
Do things move when they're not supposed to?

794
00:28:27,023 --> 00:28:28,793
Magic? Could it be a magic cafe?

795
00:28:28,793 --> 00:28:29,963
I wonder what it is.

796
00:28:30,623 --> 00:28:32,733
- Let's get out.
- Thank you.

797
00:28:32,733 --> 00:28:35,133
- Thank you for driving us.
- It was nothing.

798
00:28:35,133 --> 00:28:36,303
(They arrive at the second venue with curiosity.)

799
00:28:36,303 --> 00:28:38,903
The weather's pretty nice, considering it's summer.

800
00:28:38,903 --> 00:28:40,473
- It's tolerable.
- Yes.

801
00:28:40,473 --> 00:28:42,203
- The humidity is pretty low, so...
- Indeed.

802
00:28:42,203 --> 00:28:43,573
- It's nice and dry.
- Yes.

803
00:28:43,573 --> 00:28:45,173
- It's like the weather in LA.
- Exactly.

804
00:28:46,013 --> 00:28:47,843
- The weather in LA.
- The sun is hot,

805
00:28:47,843 --> 00:28:49,543
- but it's cool under a shade.
- Exactly.

806
00:28:50,683 --> 00:28:51,953
I love it.

807
00:28:51,953 --> 00:28:53,213
(They walk around the Hongdae area while enjoying the LA-like weather.)

808
00:28:53,213 --> 00:28:54,253
Is this us?

809
00:28:55,523 --> 00:28:57,753
- Now that the weather is nice...
- Goodness.

810
00:28:57,753 --> 00:28:59,493
- Oh, boy.
- Where are you headed?

811
00:28:59,493 --> 00:29:01,323
- I love the youthful energy.
- Yes.

812
00:29:01,323 --> 00:29:02,423
How youthful.

813
00:29:02,423 --> 00:29:04,263
- Drive safely!
- They even put on music.

814
00:29:04,263 --> 00:29:05,963
- Are you going on a trip?
- Sorry?

815
00:29:05,963 --> 00:29:07,333
- Are you going on a trip?
- Yes!

816
00:29:07,363 --> 00:29:08,903
- Have a safe trip!
- Bye!

817
00:29:09,203 --> 00:29:10,333
How lovely.

818
00:29:11,403 --> 00:29:13,533
- Wait, that's...
- "All lies."

819
00:29:13,973 --> 00:29:14,973
(I didn't know)

820
00:29:16,373 --> 00:29:17,373
I love it.

821
00:29:17,373 --> 00:29:19,113
(He loves the song.)

822
00:29:19,213 --> 00:29:20,743
I wanted to do that when I was in my 20s.

823
00:29:20,743 --> 00:29:22,113
But you couldn't.

824
00:29:22,113 --> 00:29:23,813
- I was too broke.
- You didn't have a car like that.

825
00:29:24,113 --> 00:29:26,053
How nice is that, BIBI?

826
00:29:26,053 --> 00:29:27,953
- I'm so jealous of them.
- It must be nice.

827
00:29:27,953 --> 00:29:30,383
It was like they were paid actors.

828
00:29:30,383 --> 00:29:32,023
You see a lot of these nowadays,

829
00:29:32,023 --> 00:29:33,923
but everyone stared at you when you took the top off in the past.

830
00:29:33,923 --> 00:29:35,063
- They did.
- Right?

831
00:29:35,163 --> 00:29:37,423
Back then, people looked at you strangely,

832
00:29:37,423 --> 00:29:38,563
even when you put on sunglasses.

833
00:29:38,563 --> 00:29:40,833
- They did!
- Hello.

834
00:29:40,933 --> 00:29:42,033
Hello.

835
00:29:42,033 --> 00:29:43,833
Enjoy your food!

836
00:29:44,033 --> 00:29:45,473
- Great.
- Mapo and Hongdae...

837
00:29:45,473 --> 00:29:46,733
- are certainly...
- Right.

838
00:29:46,733 --> 00:29:48,403
- youthful areas.
- Indeed.

839
00:29:48,503 --> 00:29:50,603
- I see a lot of non-Koreans.
- And surprisingly...

840
00:29:50,603 --> 00:29:51,613
(Noticing something)

841
00:29:51,613 --> 00:29:52,873
- Is this it?
- Is it?

842
00:29:55,443 --> 00:29:57,083
It just moved, right?

843
00:29:57,083 --> 00:29:58,753
What is that? It moves.

844
00:29:59,753 --> 00:30:00,883
Is this it?

845
00:30:00,883 --> 00:30:02,623
- "Coffee?"
- "Coffee?"

846
00:30:03,483 --> 00:30:04,723
Why is it...

847
00:30:04,723 --> 00:30:06,593
- opaque?
- It's opaque glass.

848
00:30:06,723 --> 00:30:08,523
Is that how it usually is,

849
00:30:08,523 --> 00:30:09,893
or did the crew do this?

850
00:30:10,093 --> 00:30:12,493
I can't tell. Don't coffee shops usually...

851
00:30:12,833 --> 00:30:14,133
- let you see...
- They're usually transparent.

852
00:30:14,133 --> 00:30:15,203
- how many people there are?
- Right.

853
00:30:15,203 --> 00:30:17,633
- It looks like an escape room.
- It does.

854
00:30:18,133 --> 00:30:19,673
It's so suspicious from the outside.

855
00:30:20,303 --> 00:30:21,803
- It's bizarre.
- A coffee shop...

856
00:30:21,803 --> 00:30:23,473
- is supposed to be...
- Right.

857
00:30:23,473 --> 00:30:24,813
It looks like they covered it.

858
00:30:24,813 --> 00:30:26,073
(It's suspicious for many reasons.)

859
00:30:26,943 --> 00:30:28,783
(What show will they watch here?)

860
00:30:28,783 --> 00:30:30,683
I see a lot of Vincent van Gogh's works.

861
00:30:30,683 --> 00:30:31,853
There are paintings.

862
00:30:31,853 --> 00:30:33,353
(There are paintings?)

863
00:30:33,683 --> 00:30:36,083
(As soon as they open the door,)

864
00:30:36,753 --> 00:30:39,093
(they see framed paintings on the wall.)

865
00:30:39,423 --> 00:30:40,553
Vincent van Gogh and...

866
00:30:40,553 --> 00:30:41,723
(And a lot of them look familiar.)

867
00:30:42,093 --> 00:30:44,263
(What do these famous paintings have to do with a show?)

868
00:30:46,363 --> 00:30:48,133
- What?
- What?

869
00:30:48,363 --> 00:30:49,463
That's so suspicious.

870
00:30:50,003 --> 00:30:51,033
What?

871
00:30:51,503 --> 00:30:52,673
It's "Mona Lisa".

872
00:30:53,273 --> 00:30:54,543
What's wrong with her arm?

873
00:30:54,543 --> 00:30:56,703
- This "Mona Lisa" is...
- It's trick art!

874
00:30:56,703 --> 00:30:57,743
(This "Mona Lisa" looks normal at first glance,)

875
00:30:58,413 --> 00:31:02,613
(but her arm is actually popping out of the painting.)

876
00:31:02,643 --> 00:31:04,553
- This "Mona Lisa" is...
- It's trick art!

877
00:31:05,053 --> 00:31:06,353
Trick art?

878
00:31:06,683 --> 00:31:08,053
Oh, I see!

879
00:31:08,053 --> 00:31:09,423
(Trick Art)

880
00:31:09,423 --> 00:31:10,753
(An art piece that uses illusion...)

881
00:31:10,753 --> 00:31:12,253
(to make a flat painting look three-dimensional)

882
00:31:12,493 --> 00:31:14,963
I think you're supposed to take pictures like this with it.

883
00:31:14,963 --> 00:31:18,033
(The greatest photo spot)

884
00:31:18,033 --> 00:31:19,833
- Don't you think?
- Great job, BIBI.

885
00:31:19,833 --> 00:31:21,503
- I didn't even think about that.
- Me neither.

886
00:31:21,503 --> 00:31:23,533
- She's so youthful.
- She really is.

887
00:31:23,633 --> 00:31:26,233
It's perfect for taking pictures.

888
00:31:27,573 --> 00:31:28,573
(Glancing)

889
00:31:28,573 --> 00:31:30,503
- Oh my goodness!
- What's wrong?

890
00:31:30,503 --> 00:31:32,113
- I was so surprised.
- What is it?

891
00:31:32,773 --> 00:31:36,743
(What's happening right now?)

892
00:31:36,743 --> 00:31:37,843
Oh my!

893
00:31:37,953 --> 00:31:39,113
Oh my gosh.

894
00:31:39,553 --> 00:31:41,083
What are we going to do with this?

895
00:31:41,183 --> 00:31:43,083
- Goodness!
- I can't...

896
00:31:43,083 --> 00:31:44,423
This is really...

897
00:31:44,623 --> 00:31:45,653
Gosh!

898
00:31:46,153 --> 00:31:47,493
I don't think...

899
00:31:48,723 --> 00:31:50,393
- So this is really...
- Wow!

900
00:31:50,463 --> 00:31:52,033
You've got to be kidding!

901
00:31:52,463 --> 00:31:54,493
This can't be real.

902
00:31:54,493 --> 00:31:56,133
There's "The Fifer" here too.

903
00:31:56,663 --> 00:31:57,733
"The Fifer".

904
00:31:58,033 --> 00:31:59,373
"Girl with a Pearl Earring".

905
00:32:00,003 --> 00:32:02,203
("Girl with a Pearl Earring" is on the other side.)

906
00:32:02,343 --> 00:32:04,243
- And that's "The Gleaners".
- "The Gleaners".

907
00:32:04,473 --> 00:32:06,543
Yes, it really is "The Gleaners".

908
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:11,513
(A Classic Paintings Cafe filled with various paintings)

909
00:32:12,013 --> 00:32:14,383
(When you pass the suspicious "Mona Lisa",)

910
00:32:15,523 --> 00:32:18,553
(you'll see the most unusual cafe you've ever seen.)

911
00:32:18,693 --> 00:32:21,023
(This is where the show takes place.)

912
00:32:21,223 --> 00:32:27,633
("The Gleaners" by Jean-Francois Millet)

913
00:32:28,033 --> 00:32:32,703
("The Fifer" by Edouard Manet)

914
00:32:33,033 --> 00:32:37,473
("Girl with a Pearl Earring" by Johannes Vermeer)

915
00:32:38,243 --> 00:32:42,243
(It's a cafe where the paintings are alive and moving.)

916
00:32:42,383 --> 00:32:45,283
So they just sit here like this for hours?

917
00:32:45,283 --> 00:32:46,453
It makes no sense.

918
00:32:46,453 --> 00:32:48,123
- Stop lying to us!
- This is fake!

919
00:32:48,123 --> 00:32:49,983
- It's way too easy.
- This is so funny.

920
00:32:49,983 --> 00:32:51,723
- This can't be real.
- Goodness.

921
00:32:51,723 --> 00:32:53,853
- This must be it.
- Look, she's laughing.

922
00:32:53,923 --> 00:32:55,163
She's holding in laughter.

923
00:32:55,293 --> 00:32:56,623
You think this is funny too, right?

924
00:32:56,823 --> 00:32:59,333
They were pushing it with this one. You have to agree.

925
00:32:59,533 --> 00:33:00,833
- Right, miss?
- Wait...

926
00:33:00,833 --> 00:33:02,633
- I mean...
- She'll have a crick in her neck.

927
00:33:02,763 --> 00:33:04,403
- She's going to hurt herself.
- Exactly!

928
00:33:05,573 --> 00:33:07,303
(Unbelievable)

929
00:33:07,773 --> 00:33:09,743
- You should change poses.
- Right.

930
00:33:09,873 --> 00:33:11,243
- You should change poses.
- Right.

931
00:33:11,543 --> 00:33:12,713
(Taking feedback in real time)

932
00:33:12,713 --> 00:33:15,583
That other pose really strains the neck.

933
00:33:16,043 --> 00:33:18,253
- Please move around.
- This is too easy.

934
00:33:18,253 --> 00:33:19,283
(Please don't stay still.)

935
00:33:19,283 --> 00:33:20,513
What is this?

936
00:33:20,753 --> 00:33:22,323
- This place...
- It's too obvious.

937
00:33:22,323 --> 00:33:23,923
- This place is perfectly fake.
- I know, right?

938
00:33:23,923 --> 00:33:26,923
- You know, Byeon Woo Seok...
- Yes?

939
00:33:27,153 --> 00:33:29,423
Woo Seok texted me the other day.

940
00:33:29,593 --> 00:33:32,893
He said his friend's cafe will be featured on this show.

941
00:33:32,893 --> 00:33:34,393
- Really?
- Could that be here?

942
00:33:34,963 --> 00:33:36,363
- He said that?
- Yes.

943
00:33:37,103 --> 00:33:38,133
Is that here?

944
00:33:38,133 --> 00:33:39,603
(Is this a real cafe owned by Byeon Woo Seok's friend?)

945
00:33:39,703 --> 00:33:42,003
Jae Seok, but this is all so suspicious.

946
00:33:42,003 --> 00:33:43,043
- We have to be careful.
- Why don't we ask?

947
00:33:43,603 --> 00:33:44,973
Woo Seok didn't tell me...

948
00:33:44,973 --> 00:33:46,343
- what kind of cafe it was.
- Right.

949
00:33:46,343 --> 00:33:47,473
(Could it be a trap Byeon Woo Seok set up with the crew?)

950
00:33:48,113 --> 00:33:49,613
Let's ask the owner.

951
00:33:49,613 --> 00:33:50,813
- Excuse me?
- Hello?

952
00:33:50,813 --> 00:33:51,913
(They decide to talk to the owner first.)

953
00:33:54,013 --> 00:33:56,853
Why is she doing this? I can't believe it.

954
00:33:57,153 --> 00:33:59,423
She's even having trouble going through the door!

955
00:34:00,623 --> 00:34:03,063
- Wait a minute.
- Stop it now!

956
00:34:03,063 --> 00:34:04,463
Don't do this to us.

957
00:34:04,493 --> 00:34:05,993
- Don't do this.
- Why?

958
00:34:05,993 --> 00:34:08,833
- Why are they taking it this far?
- I'm telling you, stop it!

959
00:34:08,933 --> 00:34:10,363
She can't go through.

960
00:34:11,263 --> 00:34:14,333
(A rectangular figure steps inside with effort.)

961
00:34:15,043 --> 00:34:17,473
(My gosh)

962
00:34:18,473 --> 00:34:19,973
Don't do this.

963
00:34:20,143 --> 00:34:22,913
- Why are they taking it this far?
- I'm telling you, stop it!

964
00:34:22,983 --> 00:34:25,513
- Hello.
- This has to be fake.

965
00:34:25,513 --> 00:34:27,213
- Right.
- Her voice is so gentle, though.

966
00:34:27,213 --> 00:34:28,753
- I'm losing my mind.
- Nice to meet you.

967
00:34:29,053 --> 00:34:31,623
Hello, I'm Oh Hui Jin. I'm 33,

968
00:34:31,623 --> 00:34:33,193
and I run this classic paintings cafe.

969
00:34:33,753 --> 00:34:35,923
It's a cafe where the subjects of classic paintings...

970
00:34:35,923 --> 00:34:38,763
greet the customers and make the drinks themselves...

971
00:34:38,763 --> 00:34:40,433
for an interactive experience.

972
00:34:40,433 --> 00:34:41,603
(A cafe where the paintings are the baristas)

973
00:34:41,763 --> 00:34:43,433
Back when I was travelling,

974
00:34:43,433 --> 00:34:45,303
I saw many street performers...

975
00:34:45,303 --> 00:34:48,643
with costumes and makeup.

976
00:34:48,643 --> 00:34:50,643
Watching them made me realise...

977
00:34:50,643 --> 00:34:53,013
I wanted to bring joy to others like them for a living too.

978
00:34:53,013 --> 00:34:54,913
That's why I started this cafe.

979
00:34:55,683 --> 00:34:57,113
At the beginning, we did...

980
00:34:57,113 --> 00:34:59,583
"Self-Portrait with Bandaged Ear" by Vincent van Gogh,

981
00:34:59,653 --> 00:35:01,823
and "Self-Portrait Dedicated to Dr. Eloesser" by Frida Kahlo.

982
00:35:01,823 --> 00:35:04,223
Those were the 2 paintings we had in Season 1, so to speak.

983
00:35:04,823 --> 00:35:07,823
Right now we're in Season Two, where we have...

984
00:35:07,823 --> 00:35:10,493
"Girl with a Pearl Earring" by Johannes Vermeer,

985
00:35:10,493 --> 00:35:12,533
"The Gleaners" by Jean-Francois Millet,

986
00:35:12,533 --> 00:35:15,233
and "The Fifer" by Edouard Manet.

987
00:35:15,563 --> 00:35:18,373
Yes, we do our makeup ourselves.

988
00:35:18,373 --> 00:35:21,333
I taught and helped my staff with their makeup at first,

989
00:35:21,333 --> 00:35:23,443
but now that they're used to it,

990
00:35:23,443 --> 00:35:25,743
they do it themselves.

991
00:35:25,743 --> 00:35:28,013
The most rewarding part is...

992
00:35:28,013 --> 00:35:29,743
when the customers come and enjoy themselves.

993
00:35:29,743 --> 00:35:31,913
And I have as much fun as they do...

994
00:35:31,913 --> 00:35:35,983
whenever I get to surprise them properly.

995
00:35:36,723 --> 00:35:37,783
I'm here!

996
00:35:37,783 --> 00:35:39,123
"Mona Lisa" is making my coffee!

997
00:35:39,123 --> 00:35:41,323
I took pictures with "The Fifer" too!

998
00:35:41,393 --> 00:35:43,023
(I went last weekend too! The coffee here is great.)

999
00:35:43,023 --> 00:35:44,393
(The cafe is already trending on social media.)

1000
00:35:45,063 --> 00:35:47,763
Sixth Sense crew, is this place real?

1001
00:35:50,133 --> 00:35:52,333
- An interactive paintings cafe?
- That's right.

1002
00:35:52,333 --> 00:35:54,473
Wait a minute...

1003
00:35:54,803 --> 00:35:56,273
I know four people are working here,

1004
00:35:56,503 --> 00:35:59,443
but you can't stay like this for hours. It's too hard.

1005
00:35:59,443 --> 00:36:02,483
We have a fixed schedule for performances like this.

1006
00:36:02,483 --> 00:36:05,083
- It's only from 1pm to 4pm.
- I see.

1007
00:36:05,183 --> 00:36:07,453
Even during the performance, we don't stay in fixed positions.

1008
00:36:07,453 --> 00:36:09,153
- We move around freely to talk...
- Oh, so you can move!

1009
00:36:09,153 --> 00:36:10,923
- and take pictures with customers.
- So you only pose...

1010
00:36:10,923 --> 00:36:12,023
- That's right.
- Okay.

1011
00:36:12,023 --> 00:36:13,153
- in between conversations.
- Yes.

1012
00:36:13,153 --> 00:36:14,523
- Then please start moving again.
- He's right.

1013
00:36:14,523 --> 00:36:16,223
- I beg you.
- You all must be tired.

1014
00:36:17,093 --> 00:36:19,493
Then do you always carry that frame on your back?

1015
00:36:19,593 --> 00:36:21,733
Yes, I try to have it on at all times.

1016
00:36:21,733 --> 00:36:23,733
We only perform a few hours a day,

1017
00:36:23,733 --> 00:36:26,103
and customers who couldn't make it in time...

1018
00:36:26,103 --> 00:36:27,403
might be disappointed.

1019
00:36:27,403 --> 00:36:28,643
So I always work with this frame.

1020
00:36:28,643 --> 00:36:30,803
You're a comedian, right?

1021
00:36:32,473 --> 00:36:34,573
- No way.
- I mean...

1022
00:36:35,113 --> 00:36:37,913
I have a feeling that you might be my junior.

1023
00:36:37,913 --> 00:36:39,683
- Are you sure?
- No, I'm not.

1024
00:36:39,953 --> 00:36:42,253
You said Byeon Woo Seok mentioned a cafe.

1025
00:36:42,253 --> 00:36:43,853
Do you happen to know Byeon Woo Seok?

1026
00:36:44,223 --> 00:36:45,653
No, I don't.

1027
00:36:45,653 --> 00:36:47,893
Is there another cafe like this?

1028
00:36:47,893 --> 00:36:49,723
- This mustn't be it.
- Right.

1029
00:36:49,993 --> 00:36:52,463
It's really cool that you're doing what you want to do in life.

1030
00:36:52,863 --> 00:36:56,263
(Is this theme-committed cafe real?)

1031
00:36:56,463 --> 00:37:00,803
(Jae Seok was looking at the part-timers.)

1032
00:37:01,033 --> 00:37:03,673
I noticed they can't stay still.

1033
00:37:04,743 --> 00:37:05,973
If you watch, they're like...

1034
00:37:05,973 --> 00:37:08,213
She's not meant for this part of the job.

1035
00:37:08,243 --> 00:37:10,313
(Back when they were talking to Hui Jin,)

1036
00:37:11,243 --> 00:37:14,313
(she kept meeting the members' eyes.)

1037
00:37:16,483 --> 00:37:18,423
(Bowing again)

1038
00:37:19,123 --> 00:37:20,753
So it seems to me...

1039
00:37:21,223 --> 00:37:24,093
this was made up suddenly to trick us.

1040
00:37:24,093 --> 00:37:25,133
- I agree.
- Right.

1041
00:37:25,133 --> 00:37:26,163
Don't you think?

1042
00:37:26,163 --> 00:37:27,593
Okay, then.

1043
00:37:27,593 --> 00:37:29,463
- Could we order some drinks first?
- Of course.

1044
00:37:29,463 --> 00:37:31,063
- Let's go to the counter.
- Thank you.

1045
00:37:31,703 --> 00:37:34,503
I really don't think she can move around with that frame.

1046
00:37:35,403 --> 00:37:37,343
- This is...
- Wow!

1047
00:37:38,543 --> 00:37:40,313
They have art lattes!

1048
00:37:40,513 --> 00:37:42,313
- Really?
- Art latte?

1049
00:37:42,313 --> 00:37:43,683
This is our signature menu.

1050
00:37:43,683 --> 00:37:44,913
(The paintings cafe's signature menu, art latte)

1051
00:37:44,913 --> 00:37:45,953
How does it work?

1052
00:37:46,083 --> 00:37:47,853
- This is your signature menu?
- Yes.

1053
00:37:47,853 --> 00:37:50,083
So we take a picture and send it to you through the QR code.

1054
00:37:50,083 --> 00:37:51,123
Then you can make a latte with that?

1055
00:37:51,123 --> 00:37:52,823
- That's right.
- Gosh.

1056
00:37:53,053 --> 00:37:54,523
- We have a printer, so...
- Goodness.

1057
00:37:54,653 --> 00:37:57,363
(Your picture taken with the painting...)

1058
00:37:57,363 --> 00:38:00,563
(becomes latte art.)

1059
00:38:00,563 --> 00:38:03,033
Should we all take a picture with "The Gleaners..."

1060
00:38:03,033 --> 00:38:04,363
- and print it on the latte?
- Gosh.

1061
00:38:04,433 --> 00:38:05,833
- Let's do it!
- Okay.

1062
00:38:06,803 --> 00:38:08,373
You look like Director Jang Hang Jun.

1063
00:38:09,003 --> 00:38:10,003
Really?

1064
00:38:10,243 --> 00:38:11,873
(Take pictures in a classic painting,)

1065
00:38:11,873 --> 00:38:13,843
So I just send you the picture like this?

1066
00:38:13,843 --> 00:38:15,283
(then send it.)

1067
00:38:15,983 --> 00:38:17,313
Should we order something else?

1068
00:38:17,713 --> 00:38:19,683
- Some cool drinks?
- I want iced americano.

1069
00:38:19,683 --> 00:38:21,213
- Goodness!
- What?

1070
00:38:22,223 --> 00:38:23,883
(One of the gleaners escaped.)

1071
00:38:23,883 --> 00:38:25,593
- Oh, gosh.
- One iced americano...

1072
00:38:26,423 --> 00:38:27,553
- My heart!
- Where are you going?

1073
00:38:27,553 --> 00:38:28,563
I have to help her.

1074
00:38:28,563 --> 00:38:30,423
- I see.
- So you come out to make drinks.

1075
00:38:30,423 --> 00:38:32,293
The others help out too.

1076
00:38:32,293 --> 00:38:33,593
One iced americano...

1077
00:38:33,593 --> 00:38:35,463
- And these are all cold, right?
- Yes.

1078
00:38:37,363 --> 00:38:39,133
It could be a production set.

1079
00:38:44,803 --> 00:38:45,843
Wait, why...

1080
00:38:46,513 --> 00:38:49,413
Why are you posing suddenly?

1081
00:38:50,013 --> 00:38:52,113
Take it easy. You can relax.

1082
00:38:53,053 --> 00:38:54,953
(Peeking)

1083
00:38:55,653 --> 00:38:57,653
I can't tell if the crew built this...

1084
00:38:57,723 --> 00:38:58,923
or if this is a real cafe.

1085
00:39:00,723 --> 00:39:01,793
Excuse me.

1086
00:39:05,163 --> 00:39:08,063
(The girl with the earring can't stay still.)

1087
00:39:08,293 --> 00:39:10,603
(This is ridiculous.)

1088
00:39:10,903 --> 00:39:11,973
What are you...

1089
00:39:13,433 --> 00:39:15,143
(I'm just posing in here.)

1090
00:39:15,143 --> 00:39:16,903
You're being the painting.

1091
00:39:17,603 --> 00:39:19,643
- You're one with the painting.
- Right.

1092
00:39:19,843 --> 00:39:21,843
This can't be an easy job.

1093
00:39:21,843 --> 00:39:23,913
- Posing, keeping up the act...
- Exactly.

1094
00:39:23,913 --> 00:39:25,383
And all the makeup.

1095
00:39:25,383 --> 00:39:26,753
I know there's a schedule,

1096
00:39:26,753 --> 00:39:28,113
but it's still hard, right?

1097
00:39:28,113 --> 00:39:29,553
- Oh, she pays you a lot?
- Really?

1098
00:39:29,653 --> 00:39:30,923
- It's good money?
- Money.

1099
00:39:30,923 --> 00:39:32,553
Then how does she make a profit?

1100
00:39:32,553 --> 00:39:33,623
Right?

1101
00:39:34,053 --> 00:39:37,293
She has to pay all her workers.

1102
00:39:37,293 --> 00:39:38,363
(BIBI thinks the salaries are too high to make a profit.)

1103
00:39:38,463 --> 00:39:40,193
But you never know these days.

1104
00:39:40,193 --> 00:39:41,933
Young folks these days...

1105
00:39:42,203 --> 00:39:44,763
might find this place enjoyable.

1106
00:39:44,763 --> 00:39:46,103
- Of course.
- Right.

1107
00:39:46,103 --> 00:39:47,773
(Pleased)

1108
00:39:47,833 --> 00:39:50,273
Do people come up and talk to you like this?

1109
00:39:50,603 --> 00:39:51,813
They do?

1110
00:39:51,813 --> 00:39:53,013
Do you reply?

1111
00:39:54,043 --> 00:39:55,183
Why don't you reply to us?

1112
00:39:59,553 --> 00:40:01,413
(Who are you talking to? I'm a painting.)

1113
00:40:01,413 --> 00:40:03,383
She went back.

1114
00:40:03,653 --> 00:40:05,323
They go back to being paintings when they're in a bind.

1115
00:40:05,693 --> 00:40:06,993
Back to being paintings.

1116
00:40:07,253 --> 00:40:09,263
- This is crazy.
- Goodness.

1117
00:40:09,623 --> 00:40:12,333
- Your drinks are ready.
- Thank you.

1118
00:40:12,333 --> 00:40:13,733
Gosh!

1119
00:40:14,063 --> 00:40:15,433
- Look!
- It's really there!

1120
00:40:15,433 --> 00:40:16,633
How does this even work?

1121
00:40:16,633 --> 00:40:18,973
It really looks like a classic painting.

1122
00:40:18,973 --> 00:40:20,333
- My goodness.
- I got it.

1123
00:40:21,503 --> 00:40:22,703
(The classic paintings cafe's signature menu)

1124
00:40:22,703 --> 00:40:24,573
- Gosh.
- I can't believe it's really there.

1125
00:40:24,943 --> 00:40:26,973
- It's just like the picture.
- This is amazing!

1126
00:40:27,073 --> 00:40:28,643
It's fascinating.

1127
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:31,043
- It really looks like a drawing.
- This is so cool.

1128
00:40:31,043 --> 00:40:32,053
(The picture is reborn as a latte.)

1129
00:40:32,053 --> 00:40:34,583
Excuse me. Here are your art lattes.

1130
00:40:34,583 --> 00:40:35,723
- So many?
- Wow!

1131
00:40:35,983 --> 00:40:37,153
What is this?

1132
00:40:37,153 --> 00:40:38,793
So these are the art lattes?

1133
00:40:39,323 --> 00:40:40,653
- This is amazing.
- Our faces are...

1134
00:40:40,653 --> 00:40:41,723
My gosh!

1135
00:40:42,593 --> 00:40:43,993
Our faces are...

1136
00:40:43,993 --> 00:40:45,633
(Special art lattes for the Sixth Sense Crew)

1137
00:40:45,763 --> 00:40:47,893
- That's me!
- It's Mona Jae Seok.

1138
00:40:48,733 --> 00:40:50,633
- This is unbelievable.
- Wait...

1139
00:40:51,003 --> 00:40:53,333
This is "Girl with a Pearl Earring".

1140
00:40:54,033 --> 00:40:56,143
It's Song Eun I with a Pearl Earring.

1141
00:40:56,773 --> 00:40:58,243
- It's Frida Kahlo!
- Frida Kahlo.

1142
00:40:58,243 --> 00:40:59,673
- That's van Gogh's self-portrait.
- Right!

1143
00:40:59,673 --> 00:41:00,773
(BIBIda Kahlo and van Kyung Pyo's self-portraits)

1144
00:41:00,973 --> 00:41:03,183
- It's so pretty!
- That's van Gogh's self-portrait.

1145
00:41:03,383 --> 00:41:05,013
This painting is perfect for you, Hyeong Seo.

1146
00:41:05,013 --> 00:41:06,013
- I really like it.
- You go well with...

1147
00:41:06,013 --> 00:41:07,413
- Frida Kahlo's art.
- It looks amazing.

1148
00:41:07,413 --> 00:41:09,183
- So cool.
- Classic painting cakes.

1149
00:41:09,183 --> 00:41:10,453
- They're beautiful!
- So pretty.

1150
00:41:10,753 --> 00:41:12,193
It's "The Starry Night" by van Gogh.

1151
00:41:12,193 --> 00:41:13,523
(Classic paintings are recreated into cakes.)

1152
00:41:13,523 --> 00:41:15,053
That's Monet's "Water Lilies".

1153
00:41:15,223 --> 00:41:16,963
- These are van Gogh too.
- Right.

1154
00:41:17,163 --> 00:41:20,333
- I have something to say.
- Yes?

1155
00:41:20,533 --> 00:41:23,503
It's impossible to sell such high-quality cakes at this cost.

1156
00:41:23,503 --> 00:41:25,403
- It doesn't make sense.
- How much were these?

1157
00:41:25,403 --> 00:41:26,433
- 19 dollars.
- Yes.

1158
00:41:26,433 --> 00:41:27,503
- It's about that much.
- So...

1159
00:41:27,503 --> 00:41:29,173
She makes the drinks, performs,

1160
00:41:29,173 --> 00:41:31,743
and bakes these cakes herself? I don't buy it.

1161
00:41:32,943 --> 00:41:35,183
(Are these high-quality yet cheap cakes fake?)

1162
00:41:35,183 --> 00:41:36,413
Should we try them?

1163
00:41:36,943 --> 00:41:38,613
The latte is delicious.

1164
00:41:38,613 --> 00:41:40,113
- It really is.
- Yes.

1165
00:41:40,583 --> 00:41:43,853
It makes me think she really owns this cafe.

1166
00:41:44,153 --> 00:41:45,893
- Everything is tasty.
- I think so too.

1167
00:41:46,153 --> 00:41:48,123
It looks silly, so I didn't expect it to be good.

1168
00:41:48,123 --> 00:41:49,223
- But...
- It's really good!

1169
00:41:49,223 --> 00:41:50,463
The taste isn't silly at all.

1170
00:41:50,463 --> 00:41:51,933
What does this mean, then?

1171
00:41:52,033 --> 00:41:54,063
- It means she really runs a cafe.
- And I think...

1172
00:41:54,063 --> 00:41:56,033
she's confident in the quality of her drinks.

1173
00:41:56,433 --> 00:41:58,363
At this point, I want to grab whoever walks by...

1174
00:41:58,363 --> 00:42:00,273
and ask them if they think this place is real.

1175
00:42:00,273 --> 00:42:01,703
But they made sure people can't look inside.

1176
00:42:01,703 --> 00:42:02,973
- Right, you can't see a thing!
- Yes.

1177
00:42:03,343 --> 00:42:05,273
Most cafes have big windows...

1178
00:42:05,273 --> 00:42:06,713
- to bring people in.
- Exactly.

1179
00:42:06,713 --> 00:42:08,043
- That's right.
- Yes.

1180
00:42:08,373 --> 00:42:09,713
- I don't...
- Someone I know...

1181
00:42:09,713 --> 00:42:11,483
But with this cafe, they can't let people see.

1182
00:42:11,483 --> 00:42:13,013
Yes, people shouldn't look inside.

1183
00:42:13,013 --> 00:42:14,013
They'll just watch and leave.

1184
00:42:14,013 --> 00:42:15,283
That can never happen.

1185
00:42:15,283 --> 00:42:17,483
It does make sense,

1186
00:42:17,483 --> 00:42:18,753
considering what you just said.

1187
00:42:18,753 --> 00:42:19,753
- Right?
- I know.

1188
00:42:19,753 --> 00:42:21,293
- This latte especially...
- Yes.

1189
00:42:21,293 --> 00:42:23,663
- He really loves that latte.
- It's so...

1190
00:42:23,663 --> 00:42:24,863
It's delicious.

1191
00:42:24,863 --> 00:42:27,233
("If it's tasty, it's real!" Yu Jae Seok)

1192
00:42:27,863 --> 00:42:29,433
This is really tricky.

1193
00:42:30,063 --> 00:42:31,233
Do you think this is fake, BIBI?

1194
00:42:31,233 --> 00:42:32,403
I really think it is.

1195
00:42:32,603 --> 00:42:34,803
They don't even have a restroom.

1196
00:42:34,803 --> 00:42:36,243
Where is the restroom?

1197
00:42:36,243 --> 00:42:39,313
The restroom is this way.

1198
00:42:39,313 --> 00:42:41,013
I see. Is there a passcode?

1199
00:42:41,013 --> 00:42:42,013
No, just go right in.

1200
00:42:42,013 --> 00:42:45,113
Does your staff use the same restroom?

1201
00:42:45,213 --> 00:42:47,013
(Of course.)

1202
00:42:48,883 --> 00:42:51,223
You smiled so kindly while talking about the restroom.

1203
00:42:51,223 --> 00:42:52,453
He's so mellow.

1204
00:42:52,593 --> 00:42:53,953
What a mellow smile.

1205
00:42:54,453 --> 00:42:56,593
- Why don't we see the last show?
- Good idea.

1206
00:42:56,593 --> 00:42:58,323
- We've seen two so far.
- Yes.

1207
00:42:58,323 --> 00:43:00,033
Then we can decide which one is fake.

1208
00:43:00,033 --> 00:43:01,133
- Sounds good.
- Okay.

1209
00:43:01,133 --> 00:43:02,133
(The gleaner sensed they were wrapping up.)

1210
00:43:02,133 --> 00:43:03,333
She went up there again.

1211
00:43:06,433 --> 00:43:07,633
This is crazy.

1212
00:43:08,573 --> 00:43:10,173
She's posing again.

1213
00:43:11,603 --> 00:43:13,313
This is like "Night at the Museum".

1214
00:43:13,313 --> 00:43:14,713
- My goodness.
- Remember at the end...

1215
00:43:14,713 --> 00:43:16,843
when everything goes back to the way it was?

1216
00:43:16,843 --> 00:43:18,143
(Everyone went back to their place.)

1217
00:43:18,213 --> 00:43:20,583
This is absurd.

1218
00:43:20,583 --> 00:43:21,653
It's so funny.

1219
00:43:21,653 --> 00:43:23,753
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

1220
00:43:23,753 --> 00:43:25,083
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1221
00:43:25,083 --> 00:43:26,823
Thank you, ma'am.

1222
00:43:27,323 --> 00:43:28,723
Thank you, ma'am.

1223
00:43:28,723 --> 00:43:30,123
(Bumping)

1224
00:43:30,123 --> 00:43:31,463
- The frame...
- Every time she bows...

1225
00:43:31,463 --> 00:43:33,863
- is hitting her!
- it hits her head!

1226
00:43:34,493 --> 00:43:35,763
I'm losing my mind.

1227
00:43:35,763 --> 00:43:37,633
It makes absolutely no sense!

1228
00:43:37,803 --> 00:43:38,903
(Awkward)

1229
00:43:38,903 --> 00:43:40,303
This is so fun.

1230
00:43:41,033 --> 00:43:42,973
- It's a really fun theme.
- Right.

1231
00:43:43,103 --> 00:43:44,303
I have no idea.

1232
00:43:44,303 --> 00:43:46,373
I can't tell if it's real or not.

1233
00:43:46,513 --> 00:43:47,773
This is so hard.

1234
00:43:48,113 --> 00:43:49,313
Shall we go?

1235
00:43:49,313 --> 00:43:51,783
(Off to the next place with great suspicion)

1236
00:43:52,113 --> 00:43:54,083
- Hello!
- Good afternoon.

1237
00:43:54,083 --> 00:43:55,783
- Hi there.
- Hello.

1238
00:43:56,123 --> 00:43:57,423
(They ran into some Gen Z on the way.)

1239
00:43:57,423 --> 00:43:58,583
Where are you headed?

1240
00:43:59,153 --> 00:44:00,593
Haidilao Hot Pot.

1241
00:44:00,593 --> 00:44:02,093
- Haidilao?
- Haidilao!

1242
00:44:02,093 --> 00:44:03,463
(The crew knows the restaurant too.)

1243
00:44:04,223 --> 00:44:06,963
(An impromptu hand-pulled noodles performance)

1244
00:44:06,963 --> 00:44:07,963
That's great.

1245
00:44:08,033 --> 00:44:10,563
(The noodles' POV)

1246
00:44:10,563 --> 00:44:12,573
- That's great.
- Kyung Pyo's good with the fans.

1247
00:44:12,573 --> 00:44:13,673
Haidilao!

1248
00:44:13,673 --> 00:44:15,073
(Perfect performance)

1249
00:44:15,443 --> 00:44:17,943
(We love you, Kyung Pyo!)

1250
00:44:18,913 --> 00:44:20,273
There are so many pretty shops.

1251
00:44:20,273 --> 00:44:21,673
- I know, right?
- It's nice.

1252
00:44:21,673 --> 00:44:24,613
It's amazing how they decorate so beautifully.

1253
00:44:24,613 --> 00:44:25,783
(The streets of Hongdae are filled with cute attractions.)

1254
00:44:25,783 --> 00:44:27,583
And it's so nice and windy today.

1255
00:44:29,183 --> 00:44:30,353
So cute.

1256
00:44:30,353 --> 00:44:31,383
(Feeling good)

1257
00:44:31,583 --> 00:44:33,253
This street makes me feel like I'm travelling abroad.

1258
00:44:33,253 --> 00:44:35,723
I know! I've never been on this street before.

1259
00:44:35,723 --> 00:44:38,063
I visit Hongdae occasionally too,

1260
00:44:38,063 --> 00:44:40,163
whether it's for a shoot or in my own time.

1261
00:44:40,493 --> 00:44:42,303
But I've never taken this route before either.

1262
00:44:42,303 --> 00:44:43,503
- Me too!
- Right.

1263
00:44:43,503 --> 00:44:44,933
Gosh, she's so youthful.

1264
00:44:44,933 --> 00:44:46,573
- Who?
- She gives off a youthful energy.

1265
00:44:46,573 --> 00:44:48,073
- How so?
- Her trendiness?

1266
00:44:48,073 --> 00:44:49,703
The colour scheme...

1267
00:44:49,703 --> 00:44:52,573
And she had a cool tattoo on her arm.

1268
00:44:53,813 --> 00:44:55,113
Hello.

1269
00:44:55,113 --> 00:44:56,113
(Walking by the trendy youngsters)

1270
00:44:56,113 --> 00:44:57,343
- Good afternoon.
- Hi.

1271
00:45:00,183 --> 00:45:01,883
I can't look at "Mona Lisa" the same way anymore.

1272
00:45:01,883 --> 00:45:04,523
- It's over there!
- My heart is pounding.

1273
00:45:04,523 --> 00:45:05,923
It says we can't trust her.

1274
00:45:05,923 --> 00:45:08,453
(A poster for a performance, "Don't trust Mona Lisa")

1275
00:45:10,093 --> 00:45:11,223
(Turning)

1276
00:45:11,223 --> 00:45:13,093
(Don't trust?)

1277
00:45:13,093 --> 00:45:14,193
Wait.

1278
00:45:14,633 --> 00:45:15,933
(What is this?)

1279
00:45:15,933 --> 00:45:18,203
Her smile is watching you.

1280
00:45:18,203 --> 00:45:19,333
Wait, is this...

1281
00:45:21,933 --> 00:45:25,773
(A poster with "Mona Lisa" is in the middle of the street?)

1282
00:45:25,773 --> 00:45:26,913
Wait, is this...

1283
00:45:27,173 --> 00:45:28,813
the B-Side?

1284
00:45:29,743 --> 00:45:31,243
You said there were hidden details.

1285
00:45:31,383 --> 00:45:32,513
(Exclaiming)

1286
00:45:32,513 --> 00:45:34,753
The hidden side!

1287
00:45:34,753 --> 00:45:36,353
- Is this it?
- Really?

1288
00:45:36,353 --> 00:45:37,553
Do you think we found it?

1289
00:45:37,553 --> 00:45:38,953
Is this like an easter egg?

1290
00:45:39,353 --> 00:45:40,553
- What do you think?
- I think so too!

1291
00:45:40,623 --> 00:45:42,823
Is this it? Is it?

1292
00:45:43,563 --> 00:45:45,733
Wait, or maybe it's an actual performance.

1293
00:45:46,533 --> 00:45:47,693
Premiering on July 7.

1294
00:45:47,993 --> 00:45:49,103
Art Hall...

1295
00:45:49,703 --> 00:45:50,903
- Faust Art Hall?
- Fouse?

1296
00:45:50,903 --> 00:45:52,303
- I don't know how to read this.
- Fox?

1297
00:45:52,733 --> 00:45:54,703
- Paus.
- Is this the B-Side?

1298
00:45:54,703 --> 00:45:55,903
This is...

1299
00:45:56,103 --> 00:45:58,273
Did we make an amazing discovery,

1300
00:45:58,913 --> 00:46:00,073
or is this a swing and a miss?

1301
00:46:01,473 --> 00:46:02,713
- It's just...
- Swinging and missing

1302
00:46:02,713 --> 00:46:05,383
(Swinging and missing)

1303
00:46:05,383 --> 00:46:07,813
(They move quickly after their short swing and a miss.)

1304
00:46:07,813 --> 00:46:09,883
- Hello.
- Good afternoon.

1305
00:46:10,253 --> 00:46:12,123
- What's that?
- It's a laser printer.

1306
00:46:12,123 --> 00:46:13,393
Gosh, this is...

1307
00:46:13,753 --> 00:46:16,023
They're printing on a wooden board.

1308
00:46:16,023 --> 00:46:17,193
(It's a laser wood shop that prints pictures on boards.)

1309
00:46:17,193 --> 00:46:18,993
What if there's a hidden clue in here too?

1310
00:46:19,293 --> 00:46:21,463
Imagine this finishes printing...

1311
00:46:21,463 --> 00:46:22,563
and the "The Fifer" is there.

1312
00:46:22,563 --> 00:46:23,863
- Gosh.
- Is this a B-Side?

1313
00:46:23,863 --> 00:46:25,133
- No way!
- Wait!

1314
00:46:25,133 --> 00:46:26,503
Don't trust "The Fifer"!

1315
00:46:26,903 --> 00:46:27,933
I'm sure it's not like that.

1316
00:46:27,933 --> 00:46:29,373
- This reminds me...
- I hope so.

1317
00:46:29,373 --> 00:46:31,473
of the oak scent from the barbecue place.

1318
00:46:32,473 --> 00:46:34,943
Why does it feel like everything is connected?

1319
00:46:34,943 --> 00:46:35,983
Right?

1320
00:46:35,983 --> 00:46:37,083
Is it?

1321
00:46:38,683 --> 00:46:41,613
(The members smell burning wood from a store they passed by.)

1322
00:46:42,583 --> 00:46:45,153
(Could this be a B-Side hidden by the production team?)

1323
00:46:45,953 --> 00:46:50,663
(They start being suspicious of everything.)

1324
00:46:50,663 --> 00:46:53,063
- We're looking really closely.
- Right?

1325
00:46:53,063 --> 00:46:54,863
- It's slowing us down.
- It's...

1326
00:46:54,863 --> 00:46:56,603
- I mean...
- We started walking really slowly.

1327
00:46:56,603 --> 00:46:59,233
I think those few coincidences...

1328
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:01,303
- really got to us.
- Yes, we can't let it overwhelm us.

1329
00:47:02,203 --> 00:47:05,443
I just found another "Mona Lisa". Is this really a coincidence?

1330
00:47:05,513 --> 00:47:07,343
I just found another "Mona Lisa".

1331
00:47:07,343 --> 00:47:09,943
Is this really a coincidence? Gosh, I'm losing my mind.

1332
00:47:09,943 --> 00:47:11,543
- It's an upside-down "Mona Lisa".
- You're right.

1333
00:47:11,543 --> 00:47:12,553
Okay.

1334
00:47:12,553 --> 00:47:14,753
(Upside-down "Mona Lisa")

1335
00:47:15,253 --> 00:47:16,923
- Students in taekwondo uniforms.
- Taekwondo?

1336
00:47:16,923 --> 00:47:18,923
