1391
00:49:03,423 --> 00:49:04,693
Is this a performance?

1392
00:49:04,693 --> 00:49:06,063
Maybe it's like break dancing.

1393
00:49:06,633 --> 00:49:08,693
- They have a mat here.
- Right?

1394
00:49:09,503 --> 00:49:11,503
(Why is there a mat on the floor?)

1395
00:49:12,103 --> 00:49:14,373
They use mats for Taekwondo too.

1396
00:49:14,473 --> 00:49:17,043
Maybe that sound was a fist hitting a punch mitt.

1397
00:49:17,943 --> 00:49:18,943
It's similar, right?

1398
00:49:18,943 --> 00:49:20,213
(The recording tape)

1399
00:49:20,213 --> 00:49:23,343
(Punch mitts)

1400
00:49:23,343 --> 00:49:27,213
- Mitts can be loud.
- It could be from an action...

1401
00:49:27,213 --> 00:49:28,383
(Shouting)

1402
00:49:29,183 --> 00:49:30,583
(Shouting)

1403
00:49:30,583 --> 00:49:32,523
I can't get used to this.

1404
00:49:32,523 --> 00:49:33,553
Goodness!

1405
00:49:33,853 --> 00:49:36,093
One, two! One, two!

1406
00:49:36,093 --> 00:49:37,393
Are they the same guys we met earlier?

1407
00:49:37,923 --> 00:49:39,993
(Coming in with loud chants...)

1408
00:49:39,993 --> 00:49:42,663
(are men in Taekwondo uniforms?)

1409
00:49:43,063 --> 00:49:44,563
- Wait!
- It's the same guys!

1410
00:49:44,763 --> 00:49:45,833
Are they?

1411
00:49:46,673 --> 00:49:47,773
Are they not?

1412
00:49:48,133 --> 00:49:50,003
- The uniform looks a bit different.
- It's not them.

1413
00:49:50,003 --> 00:49:51,373
They were younger than this.

1414
00:49:51,373 --> 00:49:52,613
- Okay.
- Yes.

1415
00:49:52,873 --> 00:49:53,873
Hold on.

1416
00:49:53,873 --> 00:49:55,943
Then did those guys just happen...

1417
00:49:55,943 --> 00:49:57,383
- to walk by us?
- Who were they?

1418
00:49:58,283 --> 00:50:01,113
(Meanwhile, the members got into their positions.)

1419
00:50:01,583 --> 00:50:02,753
This is so confusing.

1420
00:50:02,753 --> 00:50:04,153
(Shouting)

1421
00:50:04,953 --> 00:50:06,023
(Focus!)

1422
00:50:07,493 --> 00:50:10,093
(The Taekwondo performance began abruptly.)

1423
00:50:10,193 --> 00:50:11,223
Gosh.

1424
00:50:11,463 --> 00:50:12,593
This is a shop?

1425
00:50:14,863 --> 00:50:17,603
(Their Taekwondo group performance continues.)

1426
00:50:17,763 --> 00:50:19,203
- You can hear their uniforms.
- Right.

1427
00:50:21,203 --> 00:50:23,543
(Energetic)

1428
00:50:24,173 --> 00:50:25,603
(Tilting)

1429
00:50:25,843 --> 00:50:28,773
(Welcome to the Taekwondo show.)

1430
00:50:30,613 --> 00:50:31,643
(Break!)

1431
00:50:31,643 --> 00:50:32,813
Goodness.

1432
00:50:37,353 --> 00:50:38,523
It shattered into pieces!

1433
00:50:39,993 --> 00:50:41,953
(Amazed)

1434
00:50:41,953 --> 00:50:43,493
I wonder if his foot hurts.

1435
00:50:44,423 --> 00:50:45,463
This is so...

1436
00:50:48,193 --> 00:50:49,203
- My gosh.
- Goodness.

1437
00:50:54,573 --> 00:50:56,203
- My goodness.
- Gosh, it's scary.

1438
00:50:56,943 --> 00:50:59,443
- That cracking sound must be this.
- I guess so.

1439
00:50:59,443 --> 00:51:01,573
- The sound like gunshots.
- That's why it's flying around.

1440
00:51:03,113 --> 00:51:05,113
(This is basically a machine gun.)

1441
00:51:05,343 --> 00:51:07,753
(Exclaiming)

1442
00:51:07,753 --> 00:51:09,153
(Totally mesmerized)

1443
00:51:09,583 --> 00:51:11,783
(A consecutive 10-spin kick is coming up!)

1444
00:51:12,183 --> 00:51:14,793
Doesn't he get dizzy?

1445
00:51:16,793 --> 00:51:17,793
(Thank you!)

1446
00:51:18,493 --> 00:51:21,233
(Automatic round of applause)

1447
00:51:21,593 --> 00:51:23,833
- Is this a cafe?
- That does feel satisfying, though.

1448
00:51:23,833 --> 00:51:24,833
(Dazed)

1449
00:51:25,133 --> 00:51:26,773
(The show goes on.)

1450
00:51:27,133 --> 00:51:29,373
(More and more wooden boards)

1451
00:51:31,773 --> 00:51:33,513
(The K-breaking class where they smash everything)

1452
00:51:33,513 --> 00:51:35,743
So they just break them all like that.

1453
00:51:37,643 --> 00:51:38,713
(There's more!)

1454
00:51:39,653 --> 00:51:42,653
(Focused)

1455
00:51:43,723 --> 00:51:44,753
How is he going to break them?

1456
00:51:46,293 --> 00:51:48,153
(With a backflip)

1457
00:51:48,153 --> 00:51:49,163
Just like this!

1458
00:51:49,693 --> 00:51:50,763
Unbelievable!

1459
00:51:51,293 --> 00:51:52,323
That was so cool.

1460
00:51:53,933 --> 00:51:54,963
My goodness. This is...

1461
00:51:55,093 --> 00:51:56,433
- Are you the owner?
- Yes.

1462
00:51:56,763 --> 00:51:57,903
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

1463
00:51:57,903 --> 00:51:59,033
- Nice to meet you.
- Thank you for the great show.

1464
00:51:59,033 --> 00:52:00,173
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

1465
00:52:00,173 --> 00:52:01,273
We really enjoyed the show.

1466
00:52:01,273 --> 00:52:02,273
- We loved it.
- Thank you.

1467
00:52:02,273 --> 00:52:03,573
- Sir.
- Yes?

1468
00:52:03,973 --> 00:52:05,873
What kind of place is this?

1469
00:52:06,073 --> 00:52:10,683
We combined Taekwondo and a musical,

1470
00:52:10,913 --> 00:52:13,613
so you can dine while watching a show.

1471
00:52:13,613 --> 00:52:15,983
It's a Taekwondo musical pub.

1472
00:52:16,983 --> 00:52:17,983
Hello.

1473
00:52:17,983 --> 00:52:19,723
I'm Jeong Song Hwan,

1474
00:52:20,193 --> 00:52:21,823
the owner of this Taekwondo performance pub. Nice to meet you.

1475
00:52:22,693 --> 00:52:25,963
We used to train in Taekwondo together as friends,

1476
00:52:26,633 --> 00:52:28,493
and we wondered how to bring...

1477
00:52:28,493 --> 00:52:31,033
Taekwondo closer to the public.

1478
00:52:31,533 --> 00:52:34,003
Based on my experience performing...

1479
00:52:34,203 --> 00:52:37,043
in the military and overseas,

1480
00:52:39,743 --> 00:52:41,873
we decided to promote Taekwondo...

1481
00:52:41,873 --> 00:52:43,583
in a fun and exciting way.

1482
00:52:43,743 --> 00:52:45,013
(And that is how the Taekwondo show began.)

1483
00:52:45,013 --> 00:52:47,383
Our show is packed...

1484
00:52:47,383 --> 00:52:50,353
with cool board breaking and acrobatics.

1485
00:52:51,123 --> 00:52:54,053
A lot of foreign tourists visit us,

1486
00:52:54,353 --> 00:52:56,493
and we also get many families...

1487
00:52:56,493 --> 00:52:59,393
and couples on dates.

1488
00:52:59,393 --> 00:53:01,193
(A unique performance pub loved by families and couples)

1489
00:53:01,633 --> 00:53:04,863
Sixth Sense crew, do you think this place is real?

1490
00:53:04,863 --> 00:53:07,273
(Sixth Sense crew, do you think this place is real?)

1491
00:53:08,003 --> 00:53:09,803
I just don't get it.

1492
00:53:10,373 --> 00:53:12,473
- But this is...
- If I were here as a customer,

1493
00:53:12,673 --> 00:53:14,843
I wouldn't be able to focus on eating.

1494
00:53:15,343 --> 00:53:18,943
Mr. Jeong, how do customers usually react when they come here?

1495
00:53:19,483 --> 00:53:21,313
They say they leave feeling energized.

1496
00:53:21,313 --> 00:53:25,553
We also dance Taekwondo moves.

1497
00:53:25,553 --> 00:53:26,623
Okay.

1498
00:53:26,753 --> 00:53:28,593
We even do musical numbers...

1499
00:53:28,593 --> 00:53:29,693
- with a bit of acting added.
- Musical performances?

1500
00:53:29,693 --> 00:53:30,693
- Yes.
- I see.

1501
00:53:30,693 --> 00:53:32,763
(They also perform musical numbers with a touch of acting.)

1502
00:53:34,193 --> 00:53:36,503
Looking at the menu, it says...

1503
00:53:37,363 --> 00:53:39,163
A Bar of Song Tomato Pasta,

1504
00:53:39,603 --> 00:53:41,133
- Flying Kick Toowoomba Pasta, - Flying Kick Toowoomba Pasta.

1505
00:53:41,133 --> 00:53:42,643
- and Backflip Buffalo Wings.
- Backflip Buffalo Wings.

1506
00:53:43,243 --> 00:53:44,303
This is interesting.

1507
00:53:44,903 --> 00:53:46,773
Our most popular dishes are...

1508
00:53:46,773 --> 00:53:49,413
- the Flying Kick Toowoomba Pasta...
- Toowoomba.

1509
00:53:49,413 --> 00:53:53,083
and the Backflip Buffalo Wings.

1510
00:53:53,083 --> 00:53:54,853
- Then we'll have those.
- Okay.

1511
00:53:54,853 --> 00:53:56,453
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1512
00:53:56,453 --> 00:53:58,123
(Ordering the owner's recommendations)

1513
00:53:58,423 --> 00:54:00,693
(They've ordered some dishes for now, but...)

1514
00:54:00,693 --> 00:54:03,223
- Coming to the third place...
- It's more confusing, right?

1515
00:54:03,493 --> 00:54:04,563
I know. I think...

1516
00:54:04,563 --> 00:54:06,863
If I had to guess,

1517
00:54:06,933 --> 00:54:09,733
this place is... Stand-up comedy is popular these days, you know.

1518
00:54:09,733 --> 00:54:10,733
- Yes.
- A comedy venue?

1519
00:54:10,733 --> 00:54:12,463
I think they rented out...

1520
00:54:12,463 --> 00:54:13,803
- a stand-up comedy venue.
- That makes sense.

1521
00:54:13,803 --> 00:54:14,803
Right.

1522
00:54:14,803 --> 00:54:16,973
They just had to lay out mats...

1523
00:54:16,973 --> 00:54:18,673
and hire Taekwondo performers.

1524
00:54:19,073 --> 00:54:20,073
(Oh, right.)

1525
00:54:20,073 --> 00:54:22,883
(BIBI seems to have realised something.)

1526
00:54:22,883 --> 00:54:24,783
I go watch stand-up comedy all the time.

1527
00:54:24,783 --> 00:54:25,983
This place is so similar...

1528
00:54:25,983 --> 00:54:27,183
- to a stand-up comedy venue.
- It's similar, right?

1529
00:54:27,183 --> 00:54:28,283
- Exactly.
- Yes.

1530
00:54:28,383 --> 00:54:30,923
- You go everywhere, don't you?
- You really do.

1531
00:54:31,023 --> 00:54:33,323
I'm a huge stand-up comedy fan.

1532
00:54:33,323 --> 00:54:34,423
- Really?
- Yes.

1533
00:54:34,423 --> 00:54:36,223
(The new member with a packed schedule)

1534
00:54:36,993 --> 00:54:38,493
(Ding, ding)

1535
00:54:38,823 --> 00:54:40,533
- Your food is ready.
- Okay.

1536
00:54:41,593 --> 00:54:43,303
By the way, do you usually walk around barefoot like that?

1537
00:54:43,763 --> 00:54:46,103
Here are the Backflip Buffalo Wings you ordered.

1538
00:54:46,103 --> 00:54:47,473
Okay. Thank you.

1539
00:54:48,373 --> 00:54:49,873
(Where is he going?)

1540
00:54:50,503 --> 00:54:52,943
(The owner is heading to the stage after serving the food?)

1541
00:54:53,773 --> 00:54:54,813
- Again?
- My goodness.

1542
00:54:54,813 --> 00:54:56,043
Oh, dear.

1543
00:54:57,683 --> 00:54:59,383
(Busting out a backflip out of nowhere)

1544
00:54:59,653 --> 00:55:01,283
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

1545
00:55:01,283 --> 00:55:02,513
(Enjoy your meal.)

1546
00:55:03,423 --> 00:55:06,223
(What was that?)

1547
00:55:06,223 --> 00:55:08,253
This is why it's called Backflip Buffalo Wings.

1548
00:55:08,253 --> 00:55:09,253
(Ding, ding)

1549
00:55:09,563 --> 00:55:11,523
(The next dish is served.)

1550
00:55:12,323 --> 00:55:13,893
- What is this?
- This is Flying Kick Toowoomba.

1551
00:55:13,893 --> 00:55:15,633
- Flying Kick Toowoomba?
- Flying Kick Toowoomba?

1552
00:55:16,633 --> 00:55:18,563
- No, please...
- He's heading over there.

1553
00:55:18,563 --> 00:55:19,633
My goodness.

1554
00:55:20,803 --> 00:55:22,203
(The textbook flying kick)

1555
00:55:23,243 --> 00:55:24,243
(Enjoy your meal!)

1556
00:55:24,503 --> 00:55:27,113
- It is really cool, though.
- It's amazing.

1557
00:55:27,113 --> 00:55:28,943
(It is cool and absurd at the same time.)

1558
00:55:29,243 --> 00:55:31,313
(Backflip Buffalo Wings)

1559
00:55:31,643 --> 00:55:33,753
(Flying Kick Toowoomba Pasta)

1560
00:55:34,313 --> 00:55:36,053
(And many more)

1561
00:55:36,053 --> 00:55:38,023
(Single-leg turn, neck slice, 540 kick)

1562
00:55:38,883 --> 00:55:41,723
(Confused)

1563
00:55:41,723 --> 00:55:44,163
They do seem like a demonstration team, though.

1564
00:55:44,163 --> 00:55:45,663
This just doesn't make sense.

1565
00:55:45,663 --> 00:55:47,463
Wait, this was made with ramyeon.

1566
00:55:47,633 --> 00:55:48,633
- What?
- You're right.

1567
00:55:48,633 --> 00:55:49,963
They used the ramyeon noodles.

1568
00:55:50,663 --> 00:55:51,833
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1569
00:55:52,363 --> 00:55:54,203
- They are ramyeon noodles.
- It's ramyeon.

1570
00:55:54,203 --> 00:55:56,043
(The noodles in the pasta are ramyeon?)

1571
00:55:57,003 --> 00:55:59,543
- This Toowoomba ramyeon...
- It's a thing.

1572
00:55:59,543 --> 00:56:01,673
- You did a commercial for it.
- You did.

1573
00:56:01,873 --> 00:56:03,543
I'll know right away once I taste it.

1574
00:56:04,113 --> 00:56:06,983
(Tasting it right away)

1575
00:56:07,553 --> 00:56:09,683
(The other members take a bite too.)

1576
00:56:09,683 --> 00:56:10,883
To add to that,

1577
00:56:10,883 --> 00:56:12,423
it really is the ramyeon I did the commercial for.

1578
00:56:12,423 --> 00:56:13,423
It is, isn't it?

1579
00:56:13,593 --> 00:56:15,993
This is ramyeon. I love it, though.

1580
00:56:15,993 --> 00:56:17,163
(A dish made with ramyeon on the menu?)

1581
00:56:17,323 --> 00:56:19,593
- Store-bought stuff tastes best.
- Store-bought food is good.

1582
00:56:20,163 --> 00:56:22,063
It's commercially made, so it suits my taste best.

1583
00:56:22,633 --> 00:56:23,733
That's right.

1584
00:56:24,033 --> 00:56:25,803
- You do have spot-on taste buds.
- Yes.

1585
00:56:25,803 --> 00:56:28,203
The food at that first place earlier felt too fancy...

1586
00:56:28,373 --> 00:56:29,503
and was just so-so,

1587
00:56:29,803 --> 00:56:31,603
but this place is perfect for my taste.

1588
00:56:31,603 --> 00:56:32,643
(I love it here.)

1589
00:56:32,643 --> 00:56:34,573
When you go to a stand-up comedy show,

1590
00:56:34,743 --> 00:56:37,443
- they sell beer and simple drinks.
- Things are simple.

1591
00:56:37,513 --> 00:56:38,783
The food there is strictly bar snacks.

1592
00:56:38,783 --> 00:56:39,883
(The food here is just pub grub.)

1593
00:56:40,313 --> 00:56:41,813
Simple bar bites you can snack on.

1594
00:56:41,813 --> 00:56:42,983
This fits the vibe perfectly.

1595
00:56:43,683 --> 00:56:45,053
It's great food to eat...

1596
00:56:45,053 --> 00:56:47,453
- while watching the show.
- Right. With some beer.

1597
00:56:47,453 --> 00:56:49,323
- It's good, right? My goodness.
- Yes.

1598
00:56:50,193 --> 00:56:52,693
How can anyone eat like this?

1599
00:56:52,693 --> 00:56:53,763
One, two.

1600
00:56:53,763 --> 00:56:55,733
(Not a replay of earlier)

1601
00:56:55,733 --> 00:56:57,733
How many wooden boards do they break a day?

1602
00:56:58,003 --> 00:56:59,363
Wooden boards are quite pricey.

1603
00:56:59,363 --> 00:57:00,573
- All day long...
- Right.

1604
00:57:02,173 --> 00:57:05,403
(Part 2 of the show begins.)

1605
00:57:05,943 --> 00:57:07,713
(Munching)

1606
00:57:10,113 --> 00:57:11,443
How many spins is that?

1607
00:57:12,083 --> 00:57:14,213
- Didn't he do four spins?
- That was amazing.

1608
00:57:15,783 --> 00:57:16,923
(Part 2 steps up the difficulty.)

1609
00:57:18,123 --> 00:57:19,123
(Nerve-racking for viewers)

1610
00:57:19,123 --> 00:57:20,853
I was scared he might crash.

1611
00:57:21,223 --> 00:57:22,653
I feel like I'm getting indigestion.

1612
00:57:23,293 --> 00:57:24,463
(Shouting)

1613
00:57:24,723 --> 00:57:25,763
I can't believe this.

1614
00:57:25,763 --> 00:57:27,393
They keep screaming while we're eating.

1615
00:57:27,793 --> 00:57:29,903
- We can't even eat in peace.
- I know.

1616
00:57:30,303 --> 00:57:32,603
- Gosh, this is...
- There are five boards.

1617
00:57:32,803 --> 00:57:34,433
Is he breaking them while walking through the air?

1618
00:57:34,433 --> 00:57:36,273
- Exactly.
- My goodness.

1619
00:57:36,273 --> 00:57:38,673
(An ultra-high-difficulty break)

1620
00:57:39,543 --> 00:57:41,643
(So satisfying!)

1621
00:57:42,113 --> 00:57:43,943
(A five-star board break!)

1622
00:57:44,613 --> 00:57:47,483
(The grand finale break)

1623
00:57:48,713 --> 00:57:51,253
That's pretty high up. They should be careful.

1624
00:57:51,253 --> 00:57:52,283
It looks over 3m high.

1625
00:57:53,923 --> 00:57:54,953
But this is...

1626
00:57:57,293 --> 00:57:58,963
(The finishing kick)

1627
00:58:01,563 --> 00:58:02,863
- Yes!
- Attention.

1628
00:58:02,863 --> 00:58:04,163
(The thrilling Taekwondo show, the end)

1629
00:58:04,163 --> 00:58:05,163
Bow.

1630
00:58:05,163 --> 00:58:06,633
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

1631
00:58:06,973 --> 00:58:08,973
(A polite finale befitting a polite martial art)

1632
00:58:09,873 --> 00:58:11,943
(This is too hard.)

1633
00:58:12,373 --> 00:58:14,973
The vibe isn't right for eating at all.

1634
00:58:15,473 --> 00:58:17,583
- This doesn't make sense.
- Not at all.

1635
00:58:17,583 --> 00:58:19,113
- This is absurd.
- Earlier,

1636
00:58:19,113 --> 00:58:21,013
we thought the second place was definitely fake.

1637
00:58:21,013 --> 00:58:22,513
But after seeing this, it was...

1638
00:58:22,513 --> 00:58:24,223
- Exactly.
- It seems plausible now, right?

1639
00:58:24,223 --> 00:58:25,783
(Confused)

1640
00:58:25,783 --> 00:58:27,553
Isn't this place way too weird?

1641
00:58:28,153 --> 00:58:29,693
It's beyond weird. It makes no sense.

1642
00:58:30,023 --> 00:58:31,623
They didn't even clean up these broken board pieces.

1643
00:58:33,063 --> 00:58:34,693
(A view of absolute chaos)

1644
00:58:34,693 --> 00:58:37,363
And they keep locking eyes having stare-downs with customers.

1645
00:58:37,363 --> 00:58:39,533
- Then they shout.
- They scream like this.

1646
00:58:39,903 --> 00:58:41,003
(Shouting)

1647
00:58:41,003 --> 00:58:42,603
(A taste of the original)

1648
00:58:42,903 --> 00:58:44,473
To me, they seem like...

1649
00:58:45,573 --> 00:58:48,473
a very famous Taekwondo demonstration team.

1650
00:58:48,473 --> 00:58:50,113
- Right.
- Their skills are insane.

1651
00:58:50,113 --> 00:58:51,183
I think so.

1652
00:58:51,643 --> 00:58:53,913
The ceiling here is lower...

1653
00:58:53,913 --> 00:58:55,113
than where they usually perform.

1654
00:58:55,113 --> 00:58:56,623
- Exactly.
- They're adjusting to this space.

1655
00:58:56,623 --> 00:58:57,623
That's right.

1656
00:58:57,623 --> 00:58:59,423
You can't do this unless you're a real pro.

1657
00:58:59,423 --> 00:59:00,493
Exactly.

1658
00:59:00,493 --> 00:59:02,053
(Jae Seok's guess: A fake show staged with a Taekwondo demo team)

1659
00:59:02,253 --> 00:59:05,563
First of all, if the stage takes up this much space,

1660
00:59:06,263 --> 00:59:08,163
- it won't pay off.
- Exactly.

1661
00:59:08,493 --> 00:59:10,033
- I think so.
- It doesn't make sense.

1662
00:59:10,263 --> 00:59:12,263
I just don't see how they profit.

1663
00:59:12,263 --> 00:59:13,273
(This is fake! Few tables for such a spacious stage)

1664
00:59:13,273 --> 00:59:14,303
(Can they actually turn a profit?)

1665
00:59:15,233 --> 00:59:17,103
But why do I keep feeling like...

1666
00:59:17,103 --> 00:59:19,443
- this place might be real?
- Why?

1667
00:59:19,813 --> 00:59:21,113
Because of the passion.

1668
00:59:21,673 --> 00:59:24,743
- You mean the owner?
- The passion of the owner.

1669
00:59:25,443 --> 00:59:28,453
I admire that passion and applaud it,

1670
00:59:28,453 --> 00:59:29,923
but look at the mess they left behind.

1671
00:59:30,753 --> 00:59:32,223
Traces of passion.

1672
00:59:32,223 --> 00:59:33,753
I mean, this is...

1673
00:59:34,353 --> 00:59:37,493
At a place like this, the owner and staff went inside,

1674
00:59:38,663 --> 00:59:40,333
leaving all this behind...

1675
00:59:40,333 --> 00:59:43,403
The two places from earlier were almost too easy.

1676
00:59:43,903 --> 00:59:45,363
Are we heading to make our pick now?

1677
00:59:45,363 --> 00:59:46,873
(The Taekwondo show)

1678
00:59:47,133 --> 00:59:48,873
Shall we go? This is way too tough.

1679
00:59:48,873 --> 00:59:50,243
It feels so fake that it's confusing.

1680
00:59:50,643 --> 00:59:52,503
This place looks fake, too.

1681
00:59:53,413 --> 00:59:54,973
This looks like a dance studio.

1682
00:59:54,973 --> 00:59:56,743
(Sixth Sense crew suspect everything until the very end.)

1683
00:59:57,283 --> 00:59:59,753
You're right. It is a dance studio.

1684
00:59:59,753 --> 01:00:01,213
(So suspicious)

1685
01:00:01,213 --> 01:00:02,953
Shall we gather our thoughts?

1686
01:00:03,383 --> 01:00:04,623
- Shall we do that?
- Yes.

1687
01:00:05,423 --> 01:00:07,753
The four of you need to agree...

1688
01:00:07,753 --> 01:00:09,863
- We do that?
- and make one single choice.

1689
01:00:09,993 --> 01:00:11,263
As for the penalty,

1690
01:00:11,263 --> 01:00:13,493
- we thought about a few options.
- Okay.

1691
01:00:13,563 --> 01:00:16,403
If you guessed wrong two weeks in a row,

1692
01:00:16,563 --> 01:00:19,203
you could do group costume dress-ups or stuff like that.

1693
01:00:19,773 --> 01:00:21,473
- Good.
- I like that.

1694
01:00:21,473 --> 01:00:22,503
All right.

1695
01:00:22,503 --> 01:00:24,243
- We dress up after the shoot ends?
- No.

1696
01:00:24,243 --> 01:00:26,373
- During next week's shoot.
- Right from the opening?

1697
01:00:26,373 --> 01:00:27,973
Sure. It has been a bit boring, right?

1698
01:00:27,973 --> 01:00:29,143
- Okay.
- I mean, the penalty.

1699
01:00:29,213 --> 01:00:30,913
Only if we get it wrong two weeks in a row, right?

1700
01:00:30,913 --> 01:00:31,983
- All right.
- My goodness.

1701
01:00:32,413 --> 01:00:35,383
Then, Hyeong Seo, what do you think?

1702
01:00:35,683 --> 01:00:38,023
Right. You have the freshest gut feelings here.

1703
01:00:38,023 --> 01:00:39,023
That's true.

1704
01:00:39,123 --> 01:00:40,693
I think it's the second place.

1705
01:00:40,693 --> 01:00:42,453
- The second one is fake.
- It's fake?

1706
01:00:42,723 --> 01:00:47,263
The clincher is that food and drink prices...

1707
01:00:47,263 --> 01:00:49,263
- The prices?
- just don't add up.

1708
01:00:49,263 --> 01:00:50,703
- You don't think it makes sense.
- No.

1709
01:00:52,303 --> 01:00:56,003
(The place that shocked everyone)

1710
01:00:56,743 --> 01:01:00,313
(A cafe taking its concept dead seriously)

1711
01:01:01,973 --> 01:01:03,383
(Shocked by famous painting costumes,)

1712
01:01:04,443 --> 01:01:06,013
(and shocked again by masterpiece desserts)

1713
01:01:06,513 --> 01:01:08,253
(The show...)

1714
01:01:08,253 --> 01:01:10,623
(with unbelievable paintings)

1715
01:01:10,753 --> 01:01:11,783
Be honest.

1716
01:01:11,853 --> 01:01:14,453
(Which batch of comedians did you debut with?)

1717
01:01:14,653 --> 01:01:18,793
(No. 2: Classic Paintings Cafe with Painting Show)

1718
01:01:19,263 --> 01:01:21,463
(It looks like it's no. 2.)

1719
01:01:21,663 --> 01:01:22,963
What do you think, CEO Song?

1720
01:01:23,103 --> 01:01:25,803
There's a chance the second place...

1721
01:01:25,803 --> 01:01:27,873
is fake, just as Hyoung Seo said.

1722
01:01:28,973 --> 01:01:30,243
Still, I wouldn't want to eat...

1723
01:01:30,973 --> 01:01:33,113
feeling so intimidated at number three.

1724
01:01:33,743 --> 01:01:35,213
It doesn't have a restaurant vibe.

1725
01:01:36,413 --> 01:01:39,413
If it were just a spot to sit back and enjoy a show,

1726
01:01:39,413 --> 01:01:41,153
I'd get it,

1727
01:01:41,353 --> 01:01:44,753
but eating in a place that looks as if a tornado just ripped through?

1728
01:01:46,123 --> 01:01:47,753
(A Taekwondo show pub where you can dine...)

1729
01:01:48,123 --> 01:01:51,993
(while watching a performance?)

1730
01:01:52,593 --> 01:01:56,763
(Yet the concept is a bit too extreme for enjoying a meal.)

1731
01:01:56,963 --> 01:01:59,533
(Is this a fake set in a rented comedy venue...)

1732
01:02:00,203 --> 01:02:03,573
(featuring a Taekwondo demonstration team?)

1733
01:02:04,473 --> 01:02:09,273
(No. 3: Taekwondo Musical Pub featuring Taekwondo Show)

1734
01:02:09,473 --> 01:02:11,383
All right, Kyung Pyo.

1735
01:02:11,383 --> 01:02:14,183
I actually think number one is fake.

1736
01:02:14,353 --> 01:02:16,453
- He's going down a different path.
- The thing is...

1737
01:02:17,583 --> 01:02:19,523
(A fire show enjoyed...)

1738
01:02:19,523 --> 01:02:22,923
(in the heart of the city)

1739
01:02:23,863 --> 01:02:24,993
(Pouring oil all over!)

1740
01:02:25,163 --> 01:02:27,963
(A 90-dollar-range course meal served alongside a fire show)

1741
01:02:28,993 --> 01:02:30,703
(Yet the price is lower than expected,)

1742
01:02:31,363 --> 01:02:34,033
(and the chef keeps vanishing mid-cooking.)

1743
01:02:34,533 --> 01:02:38,603
(No. 1: Urban Camping Concept Restaurant featuring Fire Show)

1744
01:02:39,203 --> 01:02:40,743
(Confused)

1745
01:02:40,743 --> 01:02:42,473
I'm torn between numbers 2 and 3.

1746
01:02:43,583 --> 01:02:45,243
But number three...

1747
01:02:46,143 --> 01:02:48,653
- But think of the passion...
- The passion?

1748
01:02:48,783 --> 01:02:50,153
The passion was real,

1749
01:02:50,483 --> 01:02:53,193
but what unfolded before our eyes...

1750
01:02:53,523 --> 01:02:55,723
was just too much of a mismatch for a restaurant.

1751
01:02:55,953 --> 01:02:58,693
Above all, the Taekwondo demonstration team...

1752
01:02:58,693 --> 01:02:59,963
and the space...

1753
01:02:59,963 --> 01:03:02,333
The ceiling height needed to be much taller.

1754
01:03:02,633 --> 01:03:04,863
- It should be at least this high.
- It should be this high.

1755
01:03:04,863 --> 01:03:06,473
Actually, even this is a bit too low.

1756
01:03:06,473 --> 01:03:08,403
- It should be taller.
- As high as two floors.

1757
01:03:08,403 --> 01:03:10,143
To execute high-performance moves.

1758
01:03:11,003 --> 01:03:12,673
So, what do we do?

1759
01:03:12,673 --> 01:03:13,743
(It's time to make a decision.)

1760
01:03:13,813 --> 01:03:16,143
Should we play rock-paper-scissors again today and...

1761
01:03:16,683 --> 01:03:18,013
- That's a lot of pressure.
- That's just so...

1762
01:03:18,013 --> 01:03:19,013
But what can we do?

1763
01:03:19,013 --> 01:03:21,113
- Isn't that just a bit too absurd?
- What do we do then?

1764
01:03:21,113 --> 01:03:23,153
Then let's bestow this glorious burden...

1765
01:03:23,423 --> 01:03:25,153
- upon our newcomer...
- That's a great idea!

1766
01:03:25,883 --> 01:03:27,593
- Let Hyeong Seo decide.
- BIBI, you choose it.

1767
01:03:27,593 --> 01:03:28,753
- Let's go with Hyeong Seo's pick.
- Yes.

1768
01:03:28,753 --> 01:03:30,763
Well... I don't want to.

1769
01:03:31,663 --> 01:03:33,563
- I don't want to.
- No.

1770
01:03:33,663 --> 01:03:36,963
If we fail consecutively and end up getting a penalty,

1771
01:03:37,133 --> 01:03:38,303
we won't...

1772
01:03:38,563 --> 01:03:41,003
Then it would all be your fault.

1773
01:03:41,033 --> 01:03:42,373
(Laughing)

1774
01:03:42,373 --> 01:03:43,703
We'll just grumble about it occasionally.

1775
01:03:43,703 --> 01:03:46,473
It's your very first day today, so you go ahead and decide.

1776
01:03:47,113 --> 01:03:48,773
Okay. I've...

1777
01:03:48,773 --> 01:03:50,683
actually had my heart set on number two this whole time.

1778
01:03:50,683 --> 01:03:51,943
- Okay.
- Okay. Let's keep it simple then.

1779
01:03:51,943 --> 01:03:53,653
